// TEST: Intrinsics LGamma Non-Positive (aborts)
// ABORT: error[BL8008]
// ABORT: lgamma: argument must be positive
// ============================================================================
// lgamma is defined for x > 0 only. The reflection formula that would extend
// it to negative arguments is deliberately absent: it is a second thing to
// keep bit-identical between blade_rt::lgamma and its interpreter twin, and
// the callers this intrinsic exists for (Gamma / Poisson / Beta log-densities)
// never need it. A non-positive argument is therefore a caller bug and PANICS
// -- returning a silent NaN would let it seep into a log-likelihood and come
// out the far end as an unexplained NaN posterior.
//
// The guard is `!(x > 0.0)`, so NaN is refused on the same branch. Both the
// compiled binary (blade_rt::panic) and the interpreter (InterpPanic) raise
// BL8008 with this message, which is what the differential gate compares.
// ============================================================================
let x = 0.0 - 1.0
let bad = lgamma(x)
